{
  "id": "28",
  "name": "Manufacture of machinery and equipment n.e.c.",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Machinery makers write about AI as machine autonomy and operator assistance (autonomous tractors, haul trucks, forklifts, robots), as connected-machine services (condition monitoring, predictive maintenance, remote diagnostics) and as self-optimising process control, often justified by operator shortages. Demand effects are large: chip-making equipment for AI semiconductors, gas turbines and gensets for data center power, chillers, pumps and liquid cooling, and precision gears and screws for humanoid robots. Risks and rules include export controls on chip tools, the EU Machinery Regulation's treatment of self-evolving systems, functional safety, product liability and cyber security of connected machines.",
